To: -
Content-Type: text/html; charset=utf-8
Cache-Control: public, max-age=300

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Build a BEAM</title>
<style>
:root { color-scheme: light dark; --fg: #1d1d1f; --bg: #fbfbfd; --muted: #6e6e73; --line: #d2d2d7; --accent: #7b2ff7; }
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) { :root { --fg: #f5f5f7; --bg: #111114; --muted: #a1a1a6; --line: #3a3a3f; --accent: #b388ff; } }
body { margin: 0; background: var(--bg); color: var(--fg); font: 16px/1.5 system-ui, sans-serif; }
main { max-width: 40rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 2rem 1rem 4rem; }
h1 { margin: 0 0 .25rem; font-size: 1.75rem; }
p { margin: .5rem 0; }
.muted { color: var(--muted); font-size: .9rem; }
fieldset { border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: .5rem; margin: 1.25rem 0; padding: .75rem 1rem 1rem; }
legend { font-weight: 600; padding: 0 .25rem; }
label { display: block; margin: .75rem 0 .25rem; }
.check { display: flex; gap: .5rem; align-items: baseline; margin: .25rem 0; }
.check input { width: auto; }
input, select { box-sizing: border-box; width: 100%; padding: .5rem; font: inherit; color: inherit; background: transparent; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: .375rem; }
.row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(10rem, 1fr)); gap: 0 1rem; }
button { margin-top: 1rem; padding: .625rem 1.25rem; font: inherit; font-weight: 600; color: #fff; background: var(--accent); border: 0; border-radius: .375rem; cursor: pointer; }
.trap { position: absolute; left: -10000px; }
.sub { margin: 1rem 0 .25rem; font-weight: 600; }
.checks { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(16rem, 1fr)); gap: 0 1rem; }
.tag { display: inline-block; margin-left: .25rem; padding: 0 .4rem; font-size: .75rem; line-height: 1.4; color: var(--accent); border: 1px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 1rem; }
code { font-size: .9em; }
.nw { white-space: nowrap; }
/* The page has no script (the CSP of mkfifo.com). These rules of CSS
   use :has() in place of a script: without Elixir, the parts that need
   Elixir go away, and a choice that the build refuses shows a warning
   and turns off the button. The workflow checks each rule again. */
form:has(#elixir_version option[value=""]:checked) .needs-elixir { display: none; }
/* The parts of vix show only with vix. A hidden part still sends its
   value, and the workflow ignores a part without vix. */
.vix-parts { margin-left: 1.5rem; }
/* exqlite needs SQLite. A hidden box still sends its value, and a build
   without SQLite has no exqlite. */
form:has(#sqlite option[value="0"]:checked) .needs-sqlite { display: none; }
form:has([name=nif2]:not(:checked)) .vix-parts { display: none; }
.no-elixir, .warn { display: none; }
form:has(#elixir_version option[value=""]:checked) .no-elixir { display: block; }
.warn { margin: .5rem 0; padding: .5rem .75rem; border: 1px solid #d97706; border-radius: .375rem; color: inherit; background: rgba(217, 119, 6, .12); }
form:has([name=k_public_key]:not(:checked)):has(:is([name=k_ssl], [name=k_ssh]):checked) .w-public-key,
form:has([name=k_asn1]:not(:checked)):has(:is([name=k_public_key], [name=a_eldap]):checked) .w-asn1,
form:has(#rebar3 option[value="1"]:checked):has(:is([name=k_inets], [name=k_ssl]):not(:checked)) .w-rebar3,
form:has(#elixir_version option:not([value=""]):checked):has(#hex option[value="1"]:checked):has(:is([name=k_inets], [name=k_ssl]):not(:checked)) .w-hex { display: block; }
form:has([name=k_public_key]:not(:checked)):has(:is([name=k_ssl], [name=k_ssh]):checked) button,
form:has([name=k_asn1]:not(:checked)):has(:is([name=k_public_key], [name=a_eldap]):checked) button,
form:has(#rebar3 option[value="1"]:checked):has(:is([name=k_inets], [name=k_ssl]):not(:checked)) button,
form:has(#elixir_version option:not([value=""]):checked):has(#hex option[value="1"]:checked):has(:is([name=k_inets], [name=k_ssl]):not(:checked)) button { opacity: .45; pointer-events: none; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<main>
<h1>Build a BEAM</h1>
<p>Get a custom <a href="https://github.com/sntran/BEAM.com">beam.com</a>: Erlang/OTP and Elixir in one file that runs on Linux, macOS, Windows and the BSDs, with the parts that you choose.</p>
<p class="muted">You need no GitHub account. Choose, then select Download: the browser gets the file when its build is ready (about 2 to 3 minutes; at most 10). The address of the download is also a URL for <code>curl</code>. Or give your email address: we send a link that starts the build, and a second email gives you the file. Each file stays available for 30 days. At most 10 new builds each day.</p>

<form method="get" action="/beam.com">
<fieldset>
<legend>Erlang/OTP</legend>
<label for="otp_version">Version</label>
<select id="otp_version" name="otp_version"><option value="29.1.1" selected>29.1.1 (default)</option><option value="29.1.2">29.1.2</option><option value="29.0.6">29.0.6</option></select>
<p class="muted">beam.com always has kernel, stdlib, sasl, compiler and crypto.</p>
<input type="hidden" name="otp" value="keep">
<p class="sub">Default applications. Clear a box to leave one out, for a smaller file.</p>
<div class="checks">
<label class="check"><input type="checkbox" name="k_parsetools" value="parsetools" checked> <span>parsetools <span class="tag">default</span> <span class="muted">leex and yecc</span></span></label>
<label class="check"><input type="checkbox" name="k_asn1" value="asn1" checked> <span>asn1 <span class="tag">default</span> <span class="muted">ASN.1, for public_key</span></span></label>
<label class="check"><input type="checkbox" name="k_public_key" value="public_key" checked> <span>public_key <span class="tag">default</span> <span class="muted">certificates and keys; needs asn1</span></span></label>
<label class="check"><input type="checkbox" name="k_ssl" value="ssl" checked> <span>ssl <span class="tag">default</span> <span class="muted">TLS; needs public_key</span></span></label>
<label class="check"><input type="checkbox" name="k_inets" value="inets" checked> <span>inets <span class="tag">default</span> <span class="muted">httpc, for downloads</span></span></label>
<label class="check"><input type="checkbox" name="k_ssh" value="ssh" checked> <span>ssh <span class="tag">default</span> <span class="muted">SSH client and daemon; needs public_key</span></span></label>
<label class="check"><input type="checkbox" name="k_xmerl" value="xmerl" checked> <span>xmerl <span class="tag">default</span> <span class="muted">XML</span></span></label>
<label class="check"><input type="checkbox" name="k_runtime_tools" value="runtime_tools" checked> <span>runtime_tools <span class="tag">default</span> <span class="muted">in the apps of Phoenix</span></span></label>
<label class="check"><input type="checkbox" name="k_tools" value="tools" checked> <span>tools <span class="tag">default</span> <span class="muted">cover, for <code class="nw">mix test --cover</code></span></span></label>
</div>
<p class="sub">More applications</p>
<div class="checks">
<label class="check"><input type="checkbox" name="a_mnesia" value="mnesia"> <span>mnesia <span class="muted">database</span></span></label>
<label class="check"><input type="checkbox" name="a_os_mon" value="os_mon"> <span>os_mon <span class="muted">system monitor</span></span></label>
<label class="check"><input type="checkbox" name="a_eldap" value="eldap"> <span>eldap <span class="muted">LDAP client; needs asn1</span></span></label>
<label class="check"><input type="checkbox" name="a_ftp" value="ftp"> <span>ftp <span class="muted">FTP client</span></span></label>
<label class="check"><input type="checkbox" name="a_tftp" value="tftp"> <span>tftp <span class="muted">TFTP</span></span></label>
<label class="check"><input type="checkbox" name="a_diameter" value="diameter"> <span>diameter <span class="muted">Diameter protocol</span></span></label>
<label class="check"><input type="checkbox" name="a_eunit" value="eunit"> <span>eunit <span class="muted">unit tests</span></span></label>
<label class="check"><input type="checkbox" name="a_common_test" value="common_test"> <span>common_test <span class="muted">test framework</span></span></label>
<label class="check"><input type="checkbox" name="a_syntax_tools" value="syntax_tools"> <span>syntax_tools <span class="muted">for edoc</span></span></label>
<label class="check"><input type="checkbox" name="a_edoc" value="edoc"> <span>edoc <span class="muted">documentation; adds syntax_tools</span></span></label>
</div>
<label for="apps">Other OTP applications, with spaces</label>
<input id="apps" name="apps" placeholder="snmp megaco" maxlength="1000" pattern="([a-z][a-z0-9_]{0,63}( [a-z][a-z0-9_]{0,63}){0,39})?" autocomplete="off">
<p class="muted">Only the Erlang code of an application goes in: not its C code (as the port programs of os_mon). Hex, rebar3 and the downloads of packages need inets and ssl. A request that leaves out an application that another one needs gets an email with the reason, and no build.</p>
<div class="row">
<div><label for="jit">Emulator</label>
<select id="jit" name="jit"><option value="1">JIT (beam.com)</option><option value="0">Interpreter (beam-emu.com)</option></select></div>
<div><label for="sqlite">SQLite</label>
<select id="sqlite" name="sqlite"><option value="1">Yes</option><option value="0">No</option></select></div>
<div><label for="wasm">WebAssembly (WAMR)</label>
<select id="wasm" name="wasm"><option value="1">Yes</option><option value="0">No</option></select></div>
</div>
</fieldset>

<fieldset>
<legend>Elixir and tools</legend>
<div class="row">
<div><label for="elixir_version">Elixir</label>
<select id="elixir_version" name="elixir_version"><option value="">None</option><option value="1.20.4" selected>1.20.4 (default)</option><option value="1.20.5">1.20.5</option></select></div>
<div class="needs-elixir"><label for="hex">Hex (needs Elixir)</label>
<select id="hex" name="hex"><option value="0">No</option><option value="1">Yes</option></select></div>
<div><label for="rebar3">rebar3</label>
<select id="rebar3" name="rebar3"><option value="0">No</option><option value="1">Yes</option></select></div>
</div>
<p class="muted no-elixir">Without Elixir, the file has no Hex and no NIFs of hex.pm packages.</p>
<div class="needs-elixir">
<input type="hidden" name="dnifs" value="default">
<p class="sub">Default NIFs of hex.pm packages. Clear a box to leave one out, for a smaller file.</p>
<div class="checks">
<label class="check needs-sqlite"><input type="checkbox" name="dnif1" value="exqlite" checked> <span>exqlite <span class="tag">default</span> <span class="muted">SQLite for Elixir, for ecto_sqlite3; needs SQLite</span></span></label>
<label class="check"><input type="checkbox" name="dnif2" value="bcrypt_elixir" checked> <span>bcrypt_elixir <span class="tag">default</span> <span class="muted">for phx.gen.auth</span></span></label>
<label class="check"><input type="checkbox" name="dnif3" value="argon2_elixir" checked> <span>argon2_elixir <span class="tag">default</span> <span class="muted">for phx.gen.auth --hashing-lib argon2</span></span></label>
</div>
<p class="sub">More NIFs of hex.pm packages</p>
<p class="muted">A NIF that you do not choose adds nothing to the file.</p>
<label class="check"><input type="checkbox" name="nif1" value="picosat_elixir"> <span>picosat_elixir <span class="muted">for Ash</span></span></label>
<label class="check"><input type="checkbox" name="nif2" value="vix"> <span>vix <span class="muted">libvips, for the image package: JPEG, PNG, WebP, GIF load and PPM; about 13 MB more</span></span></label>
<div class="vix-parts">
<label class="check"><input type="checkbox" name="nif5" value="vix-icc"> <span>ICC transforms <span class="muted">lcms2; under 1 MB more</span></span></label>
<label class="check"><input type="checkbox" name="nif6" value="vix-gif"> <span>GIF save <span class="muted">cgif and libimagequant; under 1 MB more</span></span></label>
<label class="check"><input type="checkbox" name="nif7" value="vix-avif"> <span>AVIF read and write <span class="muted">libheif and aom; about 12 MB more</span></span></label>
<label class="check"><input type="checkbox" name="nif8" value="vix-svg"> <span>SVG load <span class="muted">resvg, with the fonts of the system for text; about 5.5 MB more</span></span></label>
</div>
<p class="sub">NIFs of Rust (Rustler)</p>
<p class="muted">Without one of these, the file has no Rust code.</p>
<label class="check"><input type="checkbox" name="nif3" value="rusty_csv"> <span>rusty_csv <span class="muted">CSV; about 1.3 MB more</span></span></label>
<label class="check"><input type="checkbox" name="nif4" value="ex_pdfium"> <span>ex_pdfium <span class="muted">PDF documents with PDFium; about 19 MB more</span></span></label>
</div>
</fieldset>

<p><button formnovalidate>Download</button></p>
<fieldset>
<legend>Your email address</legend>
<label for="email">We send the link and the file only to this address.</label>
<input id="email" name="email" type="email" required maxlength="254" autocomplete="email">
<div class="trap" aria-hidden="true"><label for="website">Leave this field empty</label><input id="website" name="website" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off"></div>
</fieldset>

<p class="warn w-public-key">ssl and ssh need public_key. Keep public_key, or clear ssl and ssh.</p>
<p class="warn w-asn1">public_key and eldap need asn1. Keep asn1, or clear public_key and eldap.</p>
<p class="warn w-rebar3">rebar3 needs inets and ssl. Keep inets and ssl, or choose No for rebar3.</p>
<p class="warn w-hex">Hex needs inets and ssl. Keep inets and ssl, or choose No for Hex.</p>
<button formmethod="post">Send me the link</button>
</form>
<p class="muted">A program or CI gets the file with one request: <code class="nw">curl -fo beam.com https://mkfifo.com/beam.com</code> gives the default build at once. Each choice is a field of the query: <code>otp_version</code>, <code>elixir_version</code> (empty: no Elixir), <code>apps</code>, <code>omit</code> (default applications to leave out), <code>hex</code>, <code>rebar3</code>, <code>jit</code>, <code>sqlite</code>, <code>wasm</code> (0 or 1), and <code>nifs+=</code> (the default NIFs and these) or <code>nifs=</code> (only these). For example <code class="nw">curl -fo beam.com 'https://mkfifo.com/beam.com?otp_version=29.1.2&amp;apps=mnesia&amp;nifs+=vix'</code>. The request waits for the build. <code>?nifs+=vix,rusty_csv,ex_pdfium</code> alone needs no build.</p>
<p class="muted">This page is a FIFO of <a href="https://mkfifo.com/">mkfifo.com</a>. The build runs on GitHub Actions from the main branch of BEAM.com. A member of the repository can also ask for a build with <a href="https://github.com/sntran/BEAM.com/issues/new?template=custom_build.yml">an issue</a>.</p>
</main>
</body>
</html>
